    "summary": "High‑energy June ’69 Fillmore set with epic Dark Star, The Eleven & Lovelight",
    "blurb": "The show delivers a tight, high‑octane first set that segues into an extended second half of soaring improvisations. Highlights include a blistering Dark Star, a marathon The Eleven into Turn On Your Lovelight, and a full Cryptical → Other One suite.",
    "review": "On June 5, 1969 the Grateful Dead lit up Fillmore West with one of their most electrifying performances of the era. Jerry Garcia was on fire – his soaring guitar tone and flawless vocals lifted every song, especially during Dark Star and the climactic Turn On Your Lovelight. The band’s chemistry is evident in the marathon The Eleven that rolls seamlessly into Lovelight, while the Cryptical Envelopment → Drums → The Other One → Cryptical sequence showcases their willingness to explore uncharted territory. Phil’s bass provides a rock‑solid foundation (though some listeners note a slight EQ tweak could bring out more low end), and the dual‑drummer assault from Mickey Hart and Bill Kreutzmann drives the jams forward with relentless energy. Standout moments also include hard‑rocking Hard To Handle, the playful China Cat Sunflower > Sitting On Top Of The World segue, and heartfelt renditions of Me And My Uncle and He Was A Friend Of Mine. Overall this night stands as a benchmark for the band’s late‑60s improvisational peak.",
